owing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/skye","id":88808,"login":"skye","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4ODA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Hi @mganahl \r\n\r\nIt looks like this has been resolved. I executed the mentioned code with JAX version 0.4.23 on Colab CPU and JAX version 0.3.25 on colab TPU. Now the second code mentioned also produced the output as expected.\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport os\r\nos.environ['XLA_FLAGS']='--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=4'\r\nimport jax\r\n\r\nfrom jax import pmap\r\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\n\r\nsplit_axis=0\r\nconcat_axis=0\r\nres = pmap(lambda x: jax.lax.all_to_all(x, 'i',\r\n                                        split_axis, \r\n                                        concat_axis,\r\n                                        axis_index_groups=[[0,2],[1,3]]), \r\n           axis_name='i')(np.arange(8).reshape(4,2))\r\n\r\nprint('actual')\r\nprint(np.array(res))\r\n\r\nprint('expected')\r\nprint(np.arange(8).reshape(2,2,2).transpose((2,1,0)).reshape(4,2))\r\n```\r\nOutput:\r\n```\r\nactual\r\n[[0 4]\r\n [2 6]\r\n [1 5]\r\n [3 7]]\r\nexpected\r\n[[0 4]\r\n [2 6]\r\n [1 5]\r\n [3 7]]\r\n```\r\n\r\nKindly find the gists on [CPU](https://colab.research.google.com/gist/rajasekharporeddy/f29116ca9f3b5c89fd28e34008e8000d/-cpu_5861.ipynb) and [TPU](https://colab.research.google.com/gist/rajasekharporeddy/5ce1d454760c8165b3948ecbed6734dd/-tpu_5861.ipynb) for reference.\r\n\r\nThank you","created_at":"2024-02-27T08:50:00Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/5861#issuecomment-1966058908","id":1966058908,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/5861","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc51L62c","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1966058908/reactions"},"updated_at":"2024-05-01T14:55:58Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1966058908","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/153593711?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajasekharporeddy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajasekharporeddy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajasekharporeddy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajasekharporeddy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rajasekharporeddy","id":153593711,"login":"rajasekharporeddy","node_id":"U_kgDOCSenbw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajasekharporeddy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajasekharporeddy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajasekharporeddy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajasekharporeddy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajasekharporeddy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rajasekharporeddy","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88808?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/skye","id":88808,"login":"skye","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4ODA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88808?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/skye","id":88808,"login":"skye","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4ODA4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"NONE","body":"Hi! I'm hitting some unexpected behaviour when using `all_to_all`. I'm trying to do partial swaps of a pmapped axis. The following code performes the parallel version of \r\n`np.arange(8).reshape(2,2,2).transpose((0,2,1)).reshape(4,2)`, and works as expected:\r\n\r\n```python\r\n\r\nimport os\r\nos.environ['XLA_FLAGS']='--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=4'\r\nimport jax\r\n\r\nfrom jax import pmap\r\nimport numpy as np\r\n\r\nsplit_axis=0\r\nconcat_axis=0\r\nres = pmap(lambda x: jax.lax.all_to_all(x, 'i',\r\n                                  split_axis, \r\n                                  concat_axis,\r\n                                  axis_index_groups=[[0,1],[2,3]]), \r\n           axis_name='i')(np.arange(8).reshape(4,2))\r\nprint('actual')\r\nprint(np.array(res))\r\n#[[0 2]\r\n#  [1 3]\r\n#  [4 6]\r\n#  [5 7]]\r\nprint('expected')\r\nprint(np.arange(8).reshape(2,2,2).transpose((0,2,1)).reshape(4,2))\r\n#[[0 2]\r\n#  [1 3]\r\n#  [4 6]\r\n#  [5 7]]\r\n```\r\nI believe the following code _should_ perform the parallel version of \r\n`np.arange(8).reshape(2,2,2).transpose((2,1,0)).reshape(4,2)`,\r\n```python \r\nsplit_axis=0\r\nconcat_axis=0\r\nres = pmap(lambda x: jax.lax.all_to_all(x, 'i',\r\n                                        split_axis, \r\n                                        concat_axis,\r\n                                        axis_index_groups=[[0,2],[1,3]]), \r\n           axis_name='i')(np.arange(8).reshape(4,2))\r\n\r\nprint('actual')\r\nprint(np.array(res))\r\n#[[0 4]\r\n# [3 7]\r\n# [0 4]\r\n# [3 7]]\r\nprint('expected')\r\nprint(np.arange(8).reshape(2,2,2).transpose((2,1,0)).reshape(4,2))\r\n#[[0 4]\r\n# [2 6]\r\n# [1 5]\r\n# [3 7]]\r\n```\r\nalas, it doesn't! The actual result of the second snippet is somewhat surprising to me. Maybe I'm just not using `all_to_all` properly.\r\n\r\nA side note: The same code, when run on a v3-8, actually hangs, as does `pswapaxes` for similar uses cases (`pmap`ing other functions works as expected).\r\n\r\nAny help would be greatly appreciated!\r\nthanks!\r\n\r\nedit: this could be related to #5757\r\n\r\nedit 2: This seems to be a driver issue. On a v3-8 this works with tpu_driver_nightly, but not other drivers.","closed_at":"2024-12-10T18:59:46Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88808?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/skye/followers","following_url":"https://ap